      en: "For n = 10,000 and ε = 0.1, n^(1−ε) = 10,000^0.9 ≈ 3,981. Almost each of the 10,000 points would see at least about 4,000 distinct distances. The 4-point square, with 2 distances, only shows the phenomenon at a tiny scale: the bound becomes strict when n is large.",
