      en: "With no charge, Q = 0, the inequality says r_A ≤ 2m. A horizon of radius 2 therefore forces m ≥ 1. That is Schwarzschild equality: radius 2m, mass m. With charge, the mass must be at least Q, otherwise √(m² − Q²) stops being real — the text places the same threshold.",
